.\" Part of rdratlos/racoon-ipsec-tools -- https://github.com/rdratlos/racoon-ipsec-tools
.\"
.Dd "ipsec-tools / racoon @RACOON_PACKAGE_VERSION@"
.Dt RACOON-DNS-DETECT 8
.Os
.\"
.Sh NAME
.Nm racoon-dns-detect
.Nd survey and preview the split-DNS/routing scripts' backend detection and plan
.\"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -detect | Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -explain
.Op Fl -format Ns = Ns Cm kv
.Op Fl -dns Ns = Ns Ar IP Ns Op , Ns Ar IP Ns ...
.Op Fl -domains Ns = Ns Ar DOMAIN Ns Op , Ns Ar DOMAIN Ns ...
.Op Fl -routes Ns = Ns Ar CIDR Ns Op , Ns Ar CIDR Ns ...
.Op Fl -iface Ns = Ns Ar IFACE
.Op Fl -internal-addr Ns = Ns Ar IP
.Op Fl -help
.\"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an administrator-facing diagnostic for the
.Pa phase1-up.sh Ns / Ns Pa phase1-down.sh
scripts (also called hooks) and their shared library,
.Pa racoon-hook-lib.sh ,
all shipped with this project.
None of the three have their own man pages — this page and the Admin
Guide referenced under
.Sx SEE ALSO
are their documentation.
It surveys the running system's
.Pa resolv.conf
landscape and DNS tool capabilities, classifies which backend
.Pa phase1-up.sh
would select, and — with
.Fl -dry-run —
builds and prints the exact step plan
.Pa phase1-up.sh
would apply for a given (or sample) set of Mode Config parameters.
.Pp
.Nm
never changes anything on the system: it does not require root, and it
never calls the library's apply machinery, only the survey and plan
construction that precede it.
Run it after editing
.Pa hooks.conf
or before troubleshooting a connection to see what
.Pa phase1-up.sh
would conclude without needing an active VPN session.
.\"
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -detect
Survey
.Pa resolv.conf ,
probe the DNS tool capability matrix, and classify the backend.
This is the default action.
.It Fl -dry-run
Also build and print the full step plan for the given (or sample) DNS
parameters.
Implies everything
.Fl -detect
reports.
Never executes anything.
.It Fl -explain
Include the evidence behind each conclusion — the NetworkManager
.Ic RcManager Ns / Ns Ic Mode
D-Bus property values,
.Pa nsswitch.conf
handling, which file glibc's resolver actually reads, and the detected
DNS tool's capability probe detail — instead of only the final answer.
With
.Fl -dry-run ,
also prints each step's apply and undo commands.
.It Fl -format Ns = Ns Cm kv
Emit stable
.Dq Li key=value
lines (one per line, no quoting; consumers split on the first
.Sq = )
instead of the human-readable report, for scripting.
The default format is human-readable text.
.It Fl -dns Ns = Ns Ar IP Ns Op , Ns Ar IP Ns ...
DNS server(s) to simulate with
.Fl -dry-run .
Defaults to an RFC 5737 documentation-reserved sample address if none
of
.Fl -dns , -domains ,
or
.Fl -routes
is given.
.It Fl -domains Ns = Ns Ar DOMAIN Ns Op , Ns Ar DOMAIN Ns ...
Split-DNS domain(s) to simulate with
.Fl -dry-run .
.It Fl -routes Ns = Ns Ar CIDR Ns Op , Ns Ar CIDR Ns ...
Split-include route(s) to simulate with
.Fl -dry-run .
.It Fl -iface Ns = Ns Ar IFACE
Outbound physical interface to simulate.
Defaults to
.Li eth0 ,
a placeholder — this is never auto-detected from the running system.
.It Fl -internal-addr Ns = Ns Ar IP
VPN-assigned internal address to simulate.
Defaults to an RFC 6890 documentation-reserved sample address.
.It Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.\"
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa hooks.conf
Configuration this tool reads the same way
.Pa phase1-up.sh
does — see
.Xr racoon.conf 5
and the Admin Guide.
.It Pa racoon-hook-lib.sh
The library this tool is a thin CLI wrapper over; installed alongside
.Nm
and read-only at runtime.
.El
.\"
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Exits non-zero only for an unrecognized option or a rejected
.Fl -iface Ns / Ns Fl -internal-addr
value; a completed survey or plan preview — including one that reports
a
.Ic DIVERGENT
or
.Ic PARALLEL_UNLINKED
resolv.conf landscape — always exits 0, since reporting a problem is
not itself a failure of this tool.
.\"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
.Xr racoon 8 ,
.Xr racoonctl 1
.Pp
See
.Pa doc/admin/split-dns.html
in the project source (or your distribution's documentation directory)
for the full split-DNS/routing scripts admin guide, including this tool's
own diagnostic workflow in more detail.
.\"
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was added along with the split-DNS/routing scripts for
.Xr racoon 8
roadwarrior connections.
